Use this endpoint to retrieve value rule sets within an ad account.

A rule set defines how much more certain audiences, conversion locations, and operating systems matter to your business. Our system will then optimize outcomes based on these rules.

## Request
**Endpoint** https://business-api.tiktok.com/open_api/v1.3/smart_plus/value_rule_set/get/



**Method** GET

**Header**

```xtable
|Field{30%}|Data Type{15%}|Description{55%}|
|---|---|---|
|Access-Token {Required}|string|Authorized access token. For details, see [Authentication](https://business-api.tiktok.com/portal/docs/marketing-api-authentication/v1.3). |
```

**Parameters**

```xtable
|Field{35%}|Type{15%}|Description{50%}|
|---|---|---|
|advertiser_id {Required}|string|Advertiser ID.|
|with_rules|boolean|Whether to return rule details (the object array `rules`) in the response.<br><br>Supported values: `true`, `false`.<br>Default value: `false`.|
|value_rule_set_ids|string[]|A list of rule set IDs to filter the results by.<br><br>No max size.|
```

### Example
```xcodeblock
(code curl http)
curl --location --request GET 'https://business-api.tiktok.com/open_api/v1.3/smart_plus/value_rule_set/get/?advertiser_id={{advertiser_id}}&with_rules=true' \
--header 'Access-Token: {{Access-Token}}'
(/code)
```

## Response


```xtable
|Field{30%}|Data Type{15%}|Description{55%}|
|-|-|-|
|code |number|Response code. For the complete list of response codes and descriptions, see [Appendix - Return Codes](https://business-api.tiktok.com/portal/docs/return-codes-appendix/v1.3).|
|message |string|Response message. For details, see [Appendix - Return Codes](https://business-api.tiktok.com/portal/docs/return-codes-appendix/v1.3).|
|request_id|string| The log ID of the request, which uniquely identifies a request.|
|data|object|Returned data.|
#|value_rule_sets|object[]|Details of rule sets within the ad account.|
##|create_time|string|The time when the rule set was created, in the format of `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` (UTC+0 time).<br><br>Example: `2026-01-01 00:00:01`.|
##|value_rule_set_id|string|The ID of the rule set.|
##|rule_set_name|string|The name of the rule set.|
##|rules|object[]|Details of rules in the rule set.|
###|order|number|The order of the rule in the rule set.<br><br>When you configure multiple rules in a rule set, this order indicates their priority. The system will prioritize rule application based on the rule order. If a person meets the criteria for multiple rules, we'll only apply the first applicable rule in the list.<br><br>For example:<br><br>Rule 1: Increase bid by 20% for ages 25–34 in the United States<br><br>Rule 2: Increase bid by 50% for iOS operating system<br><br>So a US-based iOS user aged 25–34 matches both rules, but only gets a 20% bid increase because Rule 1 comes first.|
###|rule_id|string|Rule ID.|
###|rule_name|string|Rule name.|
###|criteria|object[]|Details of criteria for the rule.|
####|criteria_type|string|Criterion type.<br><br>Enum values:<ul><li>`CRITERIA_TYPE_GENDER`: Genders.</li><li>`CRITERIA_TYPE_AGE`: Ages.</li><li>`CRITERIA_TYPE_LOCATION`: Locations.</li><li>`CRITERIA_TYPE_OS`: Operating systems.</li><li>`CRITERIA_TYPE_AUDIENCE`: Audience tags.</li></ul>|
####|value|object|Details of value or values for the criterion.|
#####|gender|string|Returned when `criteria_type` is `CRITERIA_TYPE_GENDER`.<br><br>Gender.<br><br>Enum values:<ul><li>`GENDER_MALE`: Male.</li><li>`GENDER_FEMALE`: Female.</li></ul>|
#####|age_groups|string[]|Returned when `criteria_type` is `CRITERIA_TYPE_AGE`.<br><br>A list of age groups.<br><br>Enum values:<ul><li>`AGE_18_24`: 18-24.</li><li>`AGE_25_34`: 25-34.</li><li>`AGE_35_44`: 35-44.</li><li>`AGE_45_54`: 45-54.</li><li>`AGE_55_100`: 55+.</li></ul>|
#####|location|object|Returned when `criteria_type` is `CRITERIA_TYPE_LOCATION`.<br><br>Details of values for the location criterion.|
######|location_ids|string[]|A list of location IDs.|
######|region_codes|string[]|A list of region codes.|
######|province_ids|string[]|A list of province IDs.|
######|city_ids|string[]|A list of city IDs.|
#####|operating_systems|string[]|Returned when `criteria_type` is `CRITERIA_TYPE_OS`.<br><br>A list of operating systems.<br><br>Enum values:<ul><li>`ANDROID`: Android.</li><li>`IOS`: iOS.</li></ul>|
#####|audience_ids|string[]|Returned when `criteria_type` is `CRITERIA_TYPE_AUDIENCE`.<br><br>A list of audience IDs.|
###|adjust_percentage|number|Bid adjustment percentage.<ul><li>For bid increases: &#91;1, 50&#93;.</li><li>For bid decreases: [-70, -1].</li></ul><br>An `adjust_percentage` of -70 represents a bid decrease of 70% when the conditions defined in `criteria` are met.|
```
